  "preamble": "Backing and devoicing of the coda alveolar tap [ɾ] to the voiceless uvular fricative [χ]. European Portuguese and the São Paulo accent keep a tap in syllable-final position (porta /ˈpɔɾ.tɐ/), but in Rio de Janeiro (Carioca) Portuguese the coda rhotic merges with the 'strong' r and is realized as a back fricative, voiceless [χ] before voiceless consonants and word-finally (porta [ˈpɔχ.tɐ], mar [ˈmaχ]). Between vowels and after onset consonants (caro, quatro) the tap is kept everywhere, so the change is confined to the syllable coda. Other Brazilian accents have glottal [h] or velar [x] in the same position.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Backing, Devoicing, Fricativization, Rhotic Neutralization",
